////////////////OBJECTIVES//////////////////


SCRIPT:MissionHint01_PotD
"Light braziers by approaching them with Aragorn to permanently reveal an area of the map"
END
SCRIPT:MissionHint02_PotD
"The spirits of the dead cause great fear to most of your heroes and units, and they will take damage over time at the sight of them."
END
SCRIPT:MissionHint03_PotD
"Kindled braziers replenish health and fallen troops over time. They also grant permanent vision and banish any wisps that approach it."
END
SCRIPT:MissionHint04_PotD
"Bring Baldor's belongings back to his corpse"
END
SCRIPT:MissionHint05_PotD
"Torches will momentarily heal nearby units"
END

////////////////Cinematic - Entry//////////////////
TEMP:HALBARADINTRO01
"This is an evil door, and my death lies beyond it. I will dare to pass it nonetheless"
END

////////////////Location: Story Shrines//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gimli073
"What is this wicked shrine they've hewn into the rock?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_elrohir067
"I wonder what secrets it holds."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine1A
"Sage: I remember when the Sea-kings came... Mighty they were, clad in bright armour, carrying long, shining swords.."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine1B
"Sage: In the face of this overwhelming glory an oath was sworn... to swear off the Dark One, \n and to aid the King of Gondor in his time of need..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine2A
"Sage: Some were glad to be rid of the Dark One's influence, and welcomed back the faith of our forebears..."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine2B
"Sage: But for others worship of the Dark One was not so easily cast aside, for their power was built upon it..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine3A
"Sage: Our King, whose name has been forgotten, soon fell back into the old rituals, the old beliefs."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine3B
"Sage: In the hour of need, when the world shook beneath the marching of great hosts, our King refused the call..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine4A
"Sage: When the Great Host crossed through our lands, we feared their wrath, sure to be delivered without mercy."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine4B
"Sage: But instead, Isildur sought out our King, and said unto him: "Thou shalt be the last king. \n And if the West prove mightier than thy Black Master..."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine4C
"Sage: ..this curse I lay upon thee and thy folk: to rest never until your oath is fulfilled. \n For this war will last through years uncounted, and you shall be summoned once again ere the end."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine5A
"Sage: Convinced of the Dark One's victory, we awaited the inevitable. Months turned into years, \n until nigh a decade later, word of the Dark One's defeat at long last reached our ears."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine5B
"Sage: Despair fell upon our people. We sought refuge inside the mountain, rarely leaving it, \n for we feared the vengeance of Gondor."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine5C
"Sage: It was during that dark time that the truth of Isildur's curse first became apparent..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine6A
"Sage: We were once numerous, but within the darkness of the mountain our people faltered. \n Our King was among the first to die, his spirit lingering restlessly beneath the mountain."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_storyshrine6B
"Sage: Soon all the rest would join him there, until at long last our once-verdant mountain \n valleys were changed to places of dark terror, where no living man dared tread..."
END

