////////////////Location: Baldor's Corpse//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn229
"Aragorn: Long ago, a Prince of Rohan ventured into this accursed mountain, \n determined to prove his courage. He never returned."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_baldor001
"Baldor: Baldor am I. At last I have been found. What news of my father? What news of our fledgling Kingdom?"
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn230
"Aragorn: Your time has long since passed, young Prince."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_baldor002
"Baldor: But it seems to me only recently that they came for me, howling from out of the darkness..."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_baldor003
"Baldor: They chased me through long corridors... I could not see my feet beneath the swirling mists."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_baldor009
"Baldor: I lost my girdle, given to me by my grandfather... by Eorl."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_baldor010
"Baldor: My brooch, too, a gift from my faithful wife... "
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_baldor011
"Baldor: ...and my helm, forged many years ago in the great Dwarf-smithies of the Grey Mountains..."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn232
"Aragorn: I must bid thee farewell, Baldor, son of Brego. May you resume your long rest in peace."
END 
SCRIPT:mgfotr_legolas113
"Perhaps this Prince of Men may find his rest once his belongings are returned to the place of his death..."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn318
"Aragorn: Perhaps the return of his heirlooms will allow his spirit to rest."
END 
SCRIPT:mgfotr_baldor012
"Baldor: ...no rest will I find... ere my death is avenged."
END 

////////////////Location: Baldor's Belongings//////////////////
SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn235
"A belt of kingly make. This must belong to Baldor."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_aragorn236
"A brooch of the House of Eorl.  We should return this to Baldor."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_legolas080
"A lofty helmet after the fashion of the ancient Northmen. The fallen prince would want this returned."
END
SCRIPT:mgfotr_elladan066
"What have you found?"
END
